# Ignore dependencies
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
.env

# A CV tailored to one company names that company. This repository is public, so a
# committed application publishes who you applied to and lets any reader enumerate the
# others. The public CV is profiles/; everything per-application lives here and leaves the
# machine only as an attached PDF. tests/ApplicationsStayLocal.test.js enforces it.
applications/
# A profile other than the published one builds beside its own file (core/GenerationTarget.js), so a build of
# profiles/general/de.json writes its PDFs and audit reports into profiles/general/out/. Nothing a build writes is
# committed, for the reason generated/.gitignore gives: Chrome stamps each print with its date, and a copy nobody
# rebuilt offers a CV older than the page (#250). applications/ is ignored whole, above. This covers where a build
# writes by default; an explicit --out is the caller's to keep out of the tree.
profiles/*/out/
